License: UNDECIDED
 No licence is declared for this source tree, and that is deliberate rather
 than an oversight: the copyright holder is developing this unlicensed until
 it is complete, and will settle the terms then. Under copyright law the
 default in that situation is that no rights are granted, so packages built
 from this tree are for local use and are not distributable as they stand.
 .
 Do not add any licence here to satisfy a lint warning, and do not copy one
 across from a sibling project. The wording of this paragraph follows
 raidcfgd, which reached the same position first.
 .
 One thing is worth knowing about the eventual choice rather than left to be
 rediscovered: this program obtains a Weather Underground API key by
 scraping it out of their own page, which their terms do not permit. That is
 recorded in project.md sec 2.2 with the reasoning, and it is a distribution
 question rather than a licensing one -- but it lands on whoever decides to
 publish a package, at the same moment.
